research:gov-esign-design.notes:
Limits of this research (2026-11-20):
1. WebSearch was unavailable from my first call. The shared budget of 200 searches per turn was already used up, so I ran no searches.
2. WebFetch could not resolve www.docusign.com or ec.europa.eu, so I tried no other non-GitHub hosts. Every page I opened in this session is on github.com, and several GitHub file pages returned HTTP 503: the Smart-ID v3 docs site, the full ARF document, the BOSA fts pom.xml and Sign&Validation.md, and the DSS cookbook. The gh API refused repositories not attached to the session.
3. The eIDAS article text, Lei 14.063 and the CCA brochure come from search-result extracts gathered in an earlier session and stored in /home/user/treegens-app/sign-and-grow/research/gaps.json. They were not re-opened here.
4. Everything marked 'prior knowledge' was not checked in this session.

The weakest parts are:
- all DocuSign counter-evidence (FedRAMP level, DocuSign France QTSP status, national eID integrations, procurement frameworks);
- Singapore, UAE and the Nordic brokers;
- German VwVfG section 3a and the Berechtigungszertifikat;
- the Decreto 10.543 account levels;
- the free-QES duty and wallet deadlines in Regulation 2024/1183.

To verify them, these hosts would need to be allowed in the environment's network settings: www.docusign.com, marketplace.fedramp.gov, ec.europa.eu, eidas.ec.europa.eu, eur-lex.europa.eu, planalto.gov.br, cca.gov.in, gesetze-im-internet.de, www.singpass.gov.sg, uaepass.ae, mitid.dk, traficom.fi, sk-eid.github.io and manual-integracao-assinatura-eletronica.readthedocs.io. More searching needs either a follow-up message or a higher CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_WEB_SEARCHES_PER_SESSION.
